DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaccll__ccrreeaattee__eennttrryy() function is a POSIX.1e call that creates a new ACL
     entry in the ACL pointed to by _a_c_l___p.  The aaccll__ccrreeaattee__eennttrryy__nnpp() function
     is a non-portable version that creates the ACL entry at position _i_n_d_e_x.
     Positions are numbered starting from zero, i.e. calling
     aaccll__ccrreeaattee__eennttrryy__nnpp() with _i_n_d_e_x argument equal to zero will prepend the
     entry to the ACL.

