     The aaccll__ccrreeaattee__eennttrryy() function returns the value 0 if successful; other‐
     wise the value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to in‐
     dicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The aaccll__ccrreeaattee__eennttrryy() function fails if:

     [EINVAL]           Argument _a_c_l___p does not point to a pointer to a valid
                        ACL.  Argument _i_n_d_e_x is out of bounds.

     [ENOMEM]           The ACL working storage requires more memory than is
                        allowed by the hardware or system-imposed memory man‐
                        agement constraints.

